{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/convexpolygonshape3d"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D\/points"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D\/godotClassName"],"generated":true}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot20ConvexPolygonShape3DC","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConvexPolygonShape3D","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ConvexPolygonShape3D","symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConvexPolygonShape3D","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Shape3D"],"type":"inheritsFrom"},{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/17SwiftGodotRuntime18VariantConvertibleP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A 3D convex polyhedron shape used for physics collision.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConvexPolygonShape3D"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A 3D convex polyhedron shape, intended for use in physics. Usually used to provide a shape for a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionShape3D"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"solid","type":"text"}]},{"text":", which means it detects collisions from objects that are fully inside it, unlike ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape3D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" which is hollow. This makes it more suitable for both detection and physics.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Convex decomposition:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A concave polyhedron can be split up into several convex polyhedra. This allows dynamic physics bodies to have complex concave collisions (at a performance cost) and can be achieved by using several "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" nodes. To generate a convex decomposition from a mesh, select the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MeshInstance3D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" node, go to the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mesh"}]},{"type":"text","text":" menu that appears above the viewport, and choose "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create Multiple Convex Collision Siblings","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Alternatively, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MeshInstance3D\/createMultipleConvexCollisions(settings:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can be called in a script to perform this decomposition at run-time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Performance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape3D"},{"type":"text","text":" is faster to check collisions against compared to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape3D"},{"type":"text","text":", but it is slower than primitive collision shapes such as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SphereShape3D"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BoxShape3D"},{"type":"text","text":". Its use should generally be limited to medium-sized objects that cannot have their collision accurately represented by primitive shapes."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/MeshInstance3D/createMultipleConvexCollisions(settings:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/meshinstance3d\/createmultipleconvexcollisions(settings:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"createMultipleConvexCollisions"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"settings"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MeshConvexDecompositionSettings","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot31MeshConvexDecompositionSettingsC"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This helper creates a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/StaticBody3D"},{"type":"text","text":" child node with m